{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92649-d20-trinity-continuum","id":92649,"title":"D20 Trinity Continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-16T21:57:36-07:00","id":92649,"title":"D20 Trinity Continuum","content":"I've never looked at the d20 books, so I am curious. Were there any changes or updates to the setting, or were the changes pure crunch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T22:15:05-07:00","id":92654,"title":"","content":"I've got the Adventure! d20 book. No updates to the setting there, just pure conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Jason, the Storyteller<br /> -<br /> &quot;Old dreams become new again in the spring. This is where the nightmares are.&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1357-storyteller31","name":"Storyteller31","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T02:56:49-07:00","id":92709,"title":"","content":"&quot;Trinity Continuum&quot; is the upcoming edition. &quot;Trinity Universe&quot; is the previous edition.<br /> <br /> Adventure! d20 was pretty much a 1:1 conversion, setting-wise. Aberrant d20 had a page or two of extra setting material -- a Proteus op reporting to Thetis that he'd overheard someone claiming to be Mercer on an Aeon Council conference call, some detail on Max's granddaughter Margaret Mercer, and so on.<br /> <br /> Trinity d20 had the most changes. All instances of the word &quot;psionic&quot; were replaced with &quot;noetic.&quot; &quot;Nippon&quot; became &quot;Nihon.&quot; The timeline was budged up to 2121-ish so that the Upeo wa Macho were available to play out of the rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T06:34:40-07:00","id":92765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92649-d20-trinity-continuum?p=92709#post92709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trinity d20 had the most changes. All instances of the word &quot;psionic&quot; were replaced with &quot;noetic.&quot; &quot;Nippon&quot; became &quot;Nihon.&quot; The timeline was budged up to 2121-ish so that the Upeo wa Macho were available to play out of the rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably for the best, given the number of &quot;Scion/psion&quot; conversations we've had...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T02:28:01-07:00","id":129742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92649-d20-trinity-continuum?p=92709#post92709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adventure! d20 was pretty much a 1:1 conversion, setting-wise. Aberrant d20 had a page or two of extra setting material -- a Proteus op reporting to Thetis that he'd overheard someone claiming to be Mercer on an Aeon Council conference call, some detail on Max's granddaughter Margaret Mercer, and so on.<br /> <br /> Trinity d20 had the most changes. All instances of the word &quot;psionic&quot; were replaced with &quot;noetic.&quot; &quot;Nippon&quot; became &quot;Nihon.&quot; The timeline was budged up to 2121-ish so that the Upeo wa Macho were available to play out of the rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, there was one change in <i>Adventure! d20 </i>\u2014 I believe I revised the costs to make Dramatic Editing a bit cheaper to use.<br /> <br /> And <i>Trinity d20 </i>also clarified biotech a bit more, distinguishing between &quot;inert&quot; (products produced via biotech processes but that aren't living things) and &quot;living&quot; (the stuff that's sort of alive and needs nutrients and whatnot). <br /> <br /> But, in the end, nothing major and not needed to pick up unless you're a serious completist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T14:34:22-07:00","id":132794,"title":"","content":"Trinity Universe d20 did indeed use cheaper costs for Dramatic Editing: there was a flat one-point cost reduction (and the insertion of a \u201croll for it\u201d step between \u201ccosts nothing\u201d and \u201ccosts one point\u201d), and there was a durther one-step reduction if the Edit in question was thematically appropriate to the character (phrased as \u201cif you have levels in class X, you get a further cost reduction if the Edit involves Y\u201d). Dramatic Editing was made available to all three lines (which is why I said \u201cTrinity Universe d20\u201d rather than \u201cAdventure d20\u201d), and Super-Science was included in both Adventure and Aberrant. <br /> <br /> ISTR something about the daredevils, mesmerists, and stalwarts in Adventure d20 favoring Intuition, Reflection, and Destruction, respectively. I\u2019d have to check the book to be sure.<br /> <br /> So no, no setting changes; but the \u201ccrunch\u201d changes were a bit more extensive than merely switching rulesets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-11-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:54:06-07:00","id":132944,"title":"","content":"Really? Dramatic Editing was made available for all three settings instead of just Adventure!? I bet my players would have loved that -- they all enjoyed having <i>phenomenal cosmic power</i> as novas and psiads, but still constantly lamented their loss of Dramatic Editing -- so much so that it's a running joke for someone, upon encountering a severe in-game problem, to say &quot;I spend a point of Inspiration to -- oh, d****t...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:55:58-07:00","id":132946,"title":"","content":"I should point out, we do this even in non-Aeonverse games.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Gangrel flies into a frenzy, lunging at you!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I spend a point of Inspiration and -- oh, F***!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T00:42:09-07:00","id":133322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92649-d20-trinity-continuum?p=132946#post132946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out, we do this even in non-Aeonverse games.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Gangrel flies into a frenzy, lunging at you!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I spend a point of Inspiration and -- oh, F***!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! That's pretty great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T12:05:09-07:00","id":134138,"title":"","content":"Adventure! D20 turns 10 years old this month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T08:44:39-07:00","id":135389,"title":"","content":"We need to bake a cake and have a party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}